## Running it without our content

`sample_data/corpora/` holds a small, redistribution-safe dataset. Start with
`SAMPLE_CONTENT_MODE=true`, or point `CONTENT_ROOT` at a content directory of
your own. Neither path needs anything in `corpora/`.

## Settled

Nothing is outstanding. Three questions that were open here have been settled:

- The 204 glossary records are Dwight Naset's work, and he released them under
  CC BY 4.0 by email on 18 September 2026. They are credited to him by name.
- The glossary's origin was never unknown — the records simply carry no
  `source` field, so the gap was in the data, not in the provenance.
- The FAQ corpus needs no per-record split. dieselsubs.com is Irving
  Greisman's own site, so records derived from it are his work and the file is
  CC BY 4.0 in full.

## What is no longer here

- Records generated from the San Francisco Maritime National Park
  Association's tour and website were removed on 2026-09-17. See
  `scripts/remove_by_source.py`.
- The Pampanito audio tour, its corpus and its audio were withdrawn on
  2026-09-17 pending the Association's permission.
- Video is not distributed here. `corpora/videos.jsonl` holds pointers to
  material hosted elsewhere, each with its own `rights_status`.
- Photographs not referenced by any record were moved out of the repository;
  only the images the lost-boat pages actually use remain.
